- Story & Context: Hiding in the abandoned Gallery 04, a renegade technician named Vani spent her shifts recalibrating the acoustic sensors to catch the "voice" of the tectonic plate shifts. She discovered that if she played the sitar against the resonant frequency of the main pipe, it sounded like a ghost pleading for air. Her fellow miners accused her of summoning a collapse, but she just kept tuning until the frequency shattered every lamp in the gallery. "The stone knows how to breathe if you strike it twice."
