Track 3: Zenith Pierces The Crust
- Story & Context: The myth persists among the underground workers that the music they created during the rescue effort eventually reached the surface, causing the mountain above them to vibrate in sympathy with their final song. Now, the survivors claim that whenever the moon is full, the pipes in the shaft begin to sing without any human touch. They leave offerings of gold dust on the conveyor belts, waiting for the mountain to finish the symphony. "I heard the zenith crack the ceiling wide open."
